# Brand Guidelines: Lean and Loaded

This document outlines the visual identity and design standards for **Lean and Loaded**. The brand balances a personal, "handwritten" touch with a clean, functional "lean" layout.

---

## 1. Brand Identity Overview
The **Lean and Loaded** identity is built on the contrast between efficiency and substance. 
* **Lean:** Represented by generous white space, minimalistic style schoolbell font typography (on canva) and glacial indiffference specifically for details and data.
* **Loaded:** Expressed through bold, handwritten headings that convey personality, warmth, and artisanal quality.

---

## 2. Colour Palette
The palette is centered on a calming baby blue, supported by professional neutrals and a soft accent.

| Element | Colour Name | Hex Code | Usage |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Primary** | **Pastel Cloud** | `#E6E7E8` | Headers, icons, and primary call-to-action buttons. |
| **Secondary** | **Deep Navy** | `#2B3A4F` | Body text, footer content, and high-contrast borders. |
| **Accent** | **Soft Coral** | `#FFADAD` | Secondary highlights and notification badges. |
| **Neutral** | **Ghost White** | `#F8F9FA` | Page backgrounds and card containers. |

---

## 3. Typography & Font Size Analysis
Based on the analysis of your brand reference image, the following sizing hierarchy is established to ensure clarity and professional structure:

| Level | Usage Example | Recommended Size | Style Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **H1: Category** | "Protein Ice Cream" | **36px / 2.25rem** | Handwritten vibes; used for major sections. |
| **H2: Product** | "#1 Choconana" | **28px / 1.75rem** | Handwritten vibes; bold weight for product titles. |
| **H3: Labels** | "Base:", "Macros" | **14px / 0.875rem** | Sans-serif; typically underlined for utility. |
| **Body: Details** | Ingredient lists | **12px / 0.75rem** | Sans-serif; clean tracking for high legibility. |
| **Footer/Small** | "Replacements" | **11px / 0.68rem** | Sans-serif; used for fine print or technical notes. |

### Font Choices
* **Handwritten Font:** *Caveat*, *Indie Flower*, or *Pacifico* (Display).
* **Sans-Serif Font:** *Inter* or *Montserrat* (UI/Functional).

---

## 4. Visual Elements & Layout
* **Spacings:** Maintain a minimum of **40px** padding between major content blocks to ensure the handwritten headings have room to breathe.
* **Iconography:** Use thin-line icons in **Pastel Cloud**. Pair with H3 labels for a scannable interface.
* **Dividers:** Use subtle, horizontal lines in **Ghost White** to separate individual product entries without adding visual "weight."

---

## 5. Front-End Implementation (CSS)
Use these variables to ensure consistency across the platform.

```css
:root {
  /* Colours */
  --primary-blue: #e6e7e8;
  --text-main: #2B3A4F;
  --accent-coral: #FFADAD;
  --bg-page: #FFFFFF;

  /* Font Sizes derived from reference */
  --size-h1: 2.25rem;   /* 36px */
  --size-h2: 1.75rem;   /* 28px */
  --size-label: 0.875rem; /* 14px */
  --size-body: 0.75rem;  /* 12px */
  --size-small: 0.68rem; /* 11px */

  /* Font Families */
  --font-display: 'Caveat', cursive;
  --font-ui: 'Inter', sans-serif;
}

h1 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--size-h1);
  color: var(--primary-blue);
  margin-bottom: 2rem;
}

.product-title {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--size-h2);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--text-main);
}

.label-text {
  font-family: var(--font-ui);
  font-size: var(--size-label);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-transform: capitalize;
}

.body-content {
  font-family: var(--font-ui);
  font-size: var(--size-body);
  line-height: 1.6;
}